{"id":"mahabharata-1-195","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":195,"title":"पञ्चनवत्यधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 195 · Bhishma counsels peace","summary":{"en":"Bhishma declares that he will never consent to war with Pandu's sons, who are as dear to him as Dhritarashtra's. He urges that half the kingdom be given to them, to wipe away the shame of the house of lac.","kn":"ಧೃತರಾಷ್ಟ್ರನ ಮಕ್ಕಳಂತೆಯೇ ತನಗೆ ಪ್ರಿಯರಾದ ಪಾಂಡುಪುತ್ರರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಯುದ್ಧಕ್ಕೆ ಎಂದೂ ಒಪ್ಪೆನೆಂದು ಭೀಷ್ಮನು ಘೋಷಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಅರಗಿನ ಮನೆಯ ಅಪಕೀರ್ತಿ ತೊಡೆದುಹಾಕಲು ಅವರಿಗೆ ಅರ್ಧ ರಾಜ್ಯ ಕೊಡಬೇಕೆಂದು ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीष्म घोषणा करते हैं कि वे पाण्डु के पुत्रों से, जो उन्हें धृतराष्ट्र के पुत्रों जितने प्रिय हैं, युद्ध के लिए कभी सहमत न होंगे। वे आग्रह करते हैं कि लाक्षागृह के कलंक को मिटाने के लिए उन्हें आधा राज्य दिया जाए।","te":"ధృతరాష్ట్రుని కుమారుల వలెనే తనకు ప్రియమైన పాండుపుత్రులతో యుద్ధానికి ఎన్నడూ అంగీకరించనని భీష్ముడు ప్రకటిస్తాడు. లక్కఇంటి అపకీర్తిని తుడిచివేయడానికి వారికి సగం రాజ్యం ఇవ్వాలని పట్టుబడతాడు.","ta":"திருதராஷ்டிரனின் மைந்தர்களைப் போலவே தமக்கு அன்புக்குரிய பாண்டுவின் மைந்தர்களுடன் போருக்கு ஒருபோதும் இசையேன் என்று பீஷ்மர் அறிவிக்கிறார். அரக்கு மாளிகையின் களங்கத்தைத் துடைக்க அவர்களுக்குப் பாதி அரசைக் கொடுக்க வேண்டும் என்று வலியுறுத்துகிறார்.","ml":"പാണ്ഡുവിന്റെ പുത്രന്മാരോട് ഒരിക്കലും യുദ്ധത്തിന് സമ്മതിക്കില്ലെന്ന് ഭീഷ്മർ പ്രഖ്യാപിക്കുന്നു; ധൃതരാഷ്ട്രരുടെ മക്കൾ പോലെ തന്നെ അവർ അദ്ദേഹത്തിന് പ്രിയപ്പെട്ടവരാണ്. അരക്കില്ലത്തിലെ അപമാനം തുടച്ചുനീക്കാൻ രാജ്യത്തിന്റെ പകുതി അവർക്ക് നൽകണമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം നിർദേശിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.195; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"विदुरागमनपर्व","titleEn":"Viduragamana Parva (Vidura's coming)","verses":[{"text":"भीष्म उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Bhishma said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"न रोचते विग्रहो मे पाण्डुपुत्रैः कथंचन ।\nयथैव धृतराष्ट्रो मे तथा पाण्डुरसंशयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I do not at all like war with the sons of Pandu. Without doubt Pandu is to me just as Dhritarashtra is."}},{"n":2,"text":"गान्धार्याश्च यथा पुत्रास्तथा कुन्तीसुता मताः ।\nयथा च मम ते रक्ष्या धृतराष्ट्र तथा तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The sons of Kunti are to be regarded as I regard Gandhari's sons. And, Dhritarashtra, they are to be protected by me and by you alike."}},{"n":3,"text":"यथा च मम राज्ञश्च तथा दुर्योधनस्य ते ।\nतथा कुरूणां सर्वेषामन्येषामपि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"As they are to me and to the king, so to Duryodhana, and so to all the Kurus and to others as well, Bharata."}},{"n":4,"text":"एवं गते विग्रहं तैर्न रोचये\nसंधाय वीरैर्दीयतामद्य भूमिः ।\nतेषामपीदं प्रपितामहानां\nराज्यं पितुश्चैव कुरूत्तमानाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"This being so, I do not like war with them. Make peace with the heroes and give them land now, for this kingdom was also that of their great-grandfathers and their father, the best of the Kurus."}},{"n":5,"text":"दुर्योधन यथा राज्यं त्वमिदं तात पश्यसि ।\nमम पैतृकमित्येवं तेऽपि पश्यन्ति पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana, as you, child, regard this kingdom as your father's inheritance, so do the Pandavas."}},{"n":6,"text":"यदि राज्यं न ते प्राप्ताः पाण्डवेयास्तपस्विनः ।\nकुत एव तवापीदं भारतस्य च कस्यचित् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If the ascetic Pandavas had not obtained the kingdom, how could you or any other Bharata have it?"}},{"n":7,"text":"अथ धर्मेण राज्यं त्वं प्राप्तवान्भरतर्षभ ।\nतेऽपि राज्यमनुप्राप्ताः पूर्वमेवेति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Or if you gained the kingdom by dharma, bull of the Bharatas, then I hold that they too had gained it earlier."}},{"n":8,"text":"मधुरेणैव राज्यस्य तेषामर्धं प्रदीयताम् ।\nएतद्धि पुरुषव्याघ्र हितं सर्वजनस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Let half the kingdom be given to them with kindness. That, tiger among men, is good for all people."}},{"n":9,"text":"अतोऽन्यथा चेत्क्रियते न हितं नो भविष्यति ।\nतवाप्यकीर्तिः सकला भविष्यति न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If it is done otherwise, it will not be good for us, and all disgrace will fall on you, without doubt."}},{"n":10,"text":"कीर्तिरक्षणमातिष्ठ कीर्तिर्हि परमं बलम् ।\nनष्टकीर्तेर्मनुष्यस्य जीवितं ह्यफलं स्मृतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Guard your reputation, for reputation is the greatest strength; for a man whose reputation is lost, life is said to be fruitless."}},{"n":11,"text":"यावत्कीर्तिर्मनुष्यस्य न प्रणश्यति कौरव ।\nतावज्जीवति गान्धारे नष्टकीर्तिस्तु नश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"As long as a man's reputation is not destroyed, Kaurava, he lives; but one whose reputation has been destroyed is destroyed."}},{"n":12,"text":"तमिमं समुपातिष्ठ धर्मं कुरुकुलोचितम् ।\nअनुरूपं महाबाहो पूर्वेषामात्मनः कुरु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Follow this dharma suited to the Kuru line, mighty-armed one, and act in a way fitting your own forefathers."}},{"n":13,"text":"दिष्ट्या धरन्ति ते वीरा दिष्ट्या जीवति सा पृथा ।\nदिष्ट्या पुरोचनः पापो नसकामोऽत्ययं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune those heroes live, by good fortune Pritha lives, and by good fortune the wicked Purochana died without getting his wish."}},{"n":14,"text":"तदा प्रभृति गान्धारे न शक्नोम्यभिवीक्षितुम् ।\nलोके प्राणभृतां कंचिच्छ्रुत्वा कुन्तीं तथागताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since then, son of Gandhari, I cannot look at any living being in the world, having heard that Kunti met such an end."}},{"n":15,"text":"न चापि दोषेण तथा लोको वैति पुरोचनम् ।\nयथा त्वां पुरुषव्याघ्र लोको दोषेण गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"And the world does not blame Purochana for the fault as it blames you, tiger among men."}},{"n":16,"text":"तदिदं जीवितं तेषां तव कल्मषनाशनम् ।\nसंमन्तव्यं महाराज पाण्डवानां च दर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So their being alive, great king, is what washes away your stain; you should accept this and the sight of the Pandavas."}},{"n":17,"text":"न चापि तेषां वीराणां जीवतां कुरुनन्दन ।\nपित्र्योंऽशः शक्य आदातुमपि वज्रभृता स्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While those heroes live, joy of the Kurus, even the wielder of the thunderbolt himself cannot take away their father's share."}},{"n":18,"text":"ते हि सर्वे स्थिता धर्मे सर्वे चैवैकचेतसः ।\nअधर्मेण निरस्ताश्च तुल्ये राज्ये विशेषतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They are all firm in dharma and all of one mind; they were cast out by injustice, especially where the kingdom was equally theirs."}},{"n":19,"text":"यदि धर्मस्त्वया कार्यो यदि कार्यं प्रियं च मे ।\nक्षेमं च यदि कर्तव्यं तेषामर्धं प्रदीयताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you must follow dharma, if you must do what pleases me, and if you want their welfare, give them half the kingdom."}}]}]}